# Credential-shaped strings that must never appear INSIDE a tracked file.
#
# The sibling file, secret-patterns, is about PATHS -- whole files that must
# not be tracked at all. This one is about content, and it exists because of
# claude/user-memory.md: that file is rewritten by Claude Code itself (a `#`
# memory-add, from any repo, during any session), so it is the one tracked
# file in here that changes without anyone opening an editor. See
# tools/check-content.sh for what this can and cannot prove.
#
# One extended-regex per line, matched against file contents. Blank lines and
# #-comments ignored. Read by BOTH .githooks/pre-commit and the CI sweep via
# tools/check-content.sh, so the local guard and the remote one cannot drift.
#
# Keep these SHAPE-based and anchored on a vendor prefix plus a length floor.
# A pattern loose enough to catch "a secret someone described in prose" is
# loose enough to fire on prose, and a guard that cries wolf gets bypassed
# with --no-verify, which is strictly worse than not having it.

# Anthropic
sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}

# OpenAI project keys (the only modern shape worth matching; a bare `sk-`
# plus hex is indistinguishable from a hash and fired on lockfiles)
sk-proj-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}

# GitHub: classic PATs/OAuth tokens are the prefix plus exactly 36, and
# fine-grained ones are github_pat_ plus a much longer body.
gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}
github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}

# GitLab
glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}

# AWS access key id
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}

# Slack
xox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}

# Private keys of any flavor, in their armored form
-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----

# An assignment whose value is long and random-looking. The length floor and
# the quoted/bare value shape are what keep this off ordinary prose: a
# sentence saying "put your token in ~/.netrc" has no `=` and no 24-char
# payload, while `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<the real thing>` has both.
(api[_-]?key|secret|passwd|password|token)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*["']?[A-Za-z0-9/+_-]{24,}
